From: Geodesic Research <noreply@geodesicresearch.org>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(hybrid): port upstream #4798 hybrid EP A2A overlap

Port of NVIDIA/Megatron-LM PR #4798, "[feat] Hybrid model ep overlapping
main" (open upstream; head 1fdff6677ec5d31a221caae491122958809d769a, 18
commits on merge-base 48a887fecd01674346f724dcf44f417f455989f0; authors
Yan Xu <yxu1@nvidia.com> and Pingtian Li <pingtianl@nvidia.com>), onto the
pinned Megatron-LM 12c20d8f0 (upstream 6cd6ea530 + the nvrx-probe carry),
with the Geodesic adaptations listed below. Combined, these let
overlap_moe_expert_parallel_comm=True (the combined-1F1B schedule) run on
Mamba/attention/MoE hybrids (HybridModel/MambaModel), not only on GPTModel.

What the upstream part adds:
- HybridModel.build_schedule_plan and a _preprocess/_postprocess split of
  HybridModel.forward (same operations, same order);
- the HybridStack fine-grained callables and schedule plan
  (models/hybrid/{fine_grained_callables,model_chunk_schedule_plan}.py);
- MambaLayer/MambaMixer backward_dw hooks;
- the bracketed HybridStack group syntax ([M*E]), with transformer-compatible
  checkpoint keys for grouped patterns;
- the hybrid MoE-layer count of training.py's MoE metrics, and the PR's
  unit tests.

What is excluded:
- The PR's first part, #4941 (PR commits 57c1bfb027..ebf43bc2da, the common
  combined-1F1B schedule-plan base), is already in the pin as upstream
  ffbe018c8. The pin's copies of the 8 files it touches are byte-identical to
  the PR at ebf43bc2da, so the rest of the PR was 3-way merged with that
  commit as the base for those files, and with 48a887fe for the others.
  Every file merged cleanly.
- The PR's changes to common/{model_chunk_schedule_plan,utils}.py,
  gpt/fine_grained_callables.py, pipeline_parallel/combined_1f1b.py,
  transformer/module.py, a2a_overlap/test_cuda_graphed_schedule_chunk_1f1b.py
  and transformer/test_submodule_callables.py all come from #4941. Those
  files merge to the pin's versions, so the port itself leaves them alone.
  Adaptation 2 below edits three of them: common/model_chunk_schedule_plan.py,
  common/utils.py and test_submodule_callables.py.
- Left out so that the pin's behaviour stands (adaptation 4): the
  is_mtp_layer flag the PR passes to MoE layers of MTP HybridStacks, and its
  router.py tracker-slot change with the test for it in test_aux_loss.py.
- Left out because adaptation 5 refuses Megatron-FSDP with the hybrid
  overlap: the PR's FSDP wiring (megatron_fsdp.py's fsdp_unit_filter, the
  adapter's HybridStack unit and unit filter, and training.py's HybridStack
  FSDP unit). Its FSDP hybrid overlap test becomes a refusal test.

Numerics and checkpoints:
- With the overlap off, a model computes what it computes at the pin: the
  forward split keeps the same operations in the same order, and MoE routers
  of MTP layers keep the pin's aux-loss scaling and logging slots.
- Flat (unbracketed) patterns keep exactly the pin's checkpoint keys
  (adaptation 3). Bracketed-group patterns, which the pin cannot build, get
  GPTModel-compatible keys, as the PR intends.

Geodesic adaptations (marked "[Geodesic adaptation]" in the code):

1. Flat-pattern grouping.
   Where: group_flat_pattern and flat_pattern_autogroup_enabled in
   models/hybrid/model_chunk_schedule_plan.py, used by
   HybridStackModelChunkSchedulePlan._build_layer_schedule_plan, and
   HybridLayerRun in models/hybrid/fine_grained_callables.py.
   Why: upstream builds one schedule unit per pattern symbol unless the
   pattern is bracketed, and bracketing builds nested stacks, which renames
   every parameter and checkpoint key. With one unit per symbol, pairing a
   forward MoE layer with a backward Mamba layer (and vice versa) leaves one
   of the two all-to-alls of each pair with no compute to hide behind.
   Change: the plan schedules each [pre-layers..., MLP/MoE] run of a flat
   pattern as one unit (Nemotron-3 Nano: 52 layers -> 23 units) without
   changing the model. MCORE_HYBRID_OVERLAP_AUTOGROUP=0 restores upstream's
   per-symbol plan; unset or 1 groups, and any other value raises.
   Effect: on a 1-node Nano smoke, -4.5% step with grouping against -2.4%
   per-symbol.
   Tests: a2a_overlap/test_hybrid_overlap.py (Nano's pattern and edge cases,
   the switch, the units a real model's plan gets, and the overlap against
   the eager model, bit for bit).

2. Experts that save their dispatched input keep it under FP8.
   Where: should_free_input in common/utils.py takes a required
   experts_quantize_input argument. experts_quantize_input in
   common/fine_grained_callables.py reads it off a layer, and
   get_layer_moe_metadata and build_hybrid_stack_callables hand it to both
   schedule plans, which pass it to their nodes; MTP nodes take it from the
   MoE layer inside the MTP layer.
   Why: upstream's should_free_input frees the mlp node's input whenever
   FP8/FP4 is on, assuming the experts saved a quantized copy of it, which
   holds for TEGroupedMLP only. Experts that run their GEMMs outside TE, such
   as Megatron-Bridge's GroupedExperts (torch._grouped_mm) or MCore's
   SequentialMLP, stay BF16 under an FP8 recipe and save the dispatched
   tokens for their weight gradient. Freeing them failed the expert backward
   with "setStorage: ... out of bounds for storage of size 0".
   Change: under FP8/FP4 only experts that quantize their input
   (TEGroupedMLP) free it; all others follow the BF16 rule. This covers
   GPTModel too: a GPT layer with non-TE experts under an FP8 recipe now
   trains through the overlap instead of failing. TEGroupedMLP layers, and
   every layer without FP8/FP4, behave as upstream.
   Tests: a2a_overlap/test_free_input_policy.py (the rule per node,
   dispatcher and expert kind; the metadata of real TE, local, dense and MTP
   layers; a GPT layer with SequentialMLP experts under FP8 through the
   overlap schedule, bit-exact against the reference, which fails with
   upstream's rule).

3. Flat patterns keep the output layer's extra state in checkpoints.
   Where: HybridModel.sharded_state_dict.
   Why: the PR drops output_layer._extra_state from every HybridModel's
   sharded state dict, to match GPTModel. For flat patterns that contradicts
   the PR's own rule that only bracketed-group patterns take GPTModel's keys,
   and a checkpoint saved that way cannot be loaded strictly by a tree
   without the port ("Missing key in checkpoint state_dict:
   output_layer._extra_state/shard_0_1").
   Change: the key is dropped only for bracketed-group patterns
   (HybridStack.transformer_sharded_keys).
   Tests: models/test_hybrid_model.py,
   test_flat_pattern_checkpoint_keys_match_the_pin (the checkpoint keys of a
   flat Mamba/attention/MLP model and of a Nano-shaped flat MoE model equal
   those the pin produces; fails with the PR's rule).

4. The pin's behaviour where the PR changes it with the overlap off.
   - MoE layers of MTP HybridStacks are built without is_mtp_layer, and
     router.py is the pin's. With the PR's flag, the routers of a
     repeated-layer MTP model (mtp_use_repeated_layer) divide their aux loss
     by mtp_num_layers, and the PR's tracker-slot formula sends every MTP
     depth to one slot, because the layer number restarts at each depth.
   - HybridModel._preprocess returns sequence_len_offset as None; HybridStack
     builds it for flash-decode / local-cudagraph static-batching inference,
     as at the pin. The PR's version read the batch size from input_ids,
     which fails when only decoder_input is passed, and allocated an unused
     tensor at every step.
   Tests: models/test_hybrid_model.py (the MoE router of a hybrid MTP model;
   _preprocess with decoder_input and no input_ids under static batching),
   both failing on the PR's code, and test_hybrid_overlap.py's MTP
   overlap-vs-eager comparison.

5. Settings the hybrid schedule refuses.
   check_hybrid_overlap_supported (models/hybrid/model_chunk_schedule_plan.py)
   runs when the plan is built and raises for:
   - the flex dispatcher's ncclep backend: the hybrid dispatch and expert
     nodes detach the probs and hold tokens_per_expert only for deepep and
     hybridep;
   - fine_grained_activation_offloading: the hybrid combine node does not
     offload the mlp_norm output (the PR called a method the pin lacks);
   - delay_wgrad_compute: the hybrid pre-dispatch node schedules the MoE
     layer's pre-dispatch weight gradients only when it has shared experts,
     so a latent MoE layer without them never computes fc1_latent_proj's
     weight gradient.
   The Megatron-FSDP adapter raises for overlap_moe_expert_parallel_comm on
   a model that contains HybridStacks: the hybrid schedule units are not
   reached by its unit discovery and reshard hooks.
   Tests: a2a_overlap/test_hybrid_overlap.py (each refusal, the supported
   dispatchers, and build_schedule_plan refusing before it builds anything)
   and a2a_overlap/test_fsdp_hybrid_overlap.py (the FSDP refusal, and a
   hybrid model wrapped as before without the overlap).

Validation (Geodesic, 2026-09-29), all on Nemotron-3 Nano 30B-A3B pretraining
in the champion posture (flex/HybridEP dispatcher, torch_grouped experts,
moe_act recompute, FP8 current scaling on the dense layers):
- 1-node smokes at 11 and 21 layers, overlap ON vs OFF: iterations 1-2 are
  bit-identical, and ON-vs-OFF loss differences stay inside the OFF-vs-OFF
  band.
- 64 GPUs: 5.197 and 5.228 s/iter with the overlap against 5.388-5.409 s
  without, i.e. -3.4% (Geodesic campaign entry E-044). Those runs used a
  tree with adaptations 1 and 2 in an earlier form and without adaptations
  3-5. Deterministic 1-node smokes of that posture (11 layers, overlap on)
  give identical loss and grad norm at every iteration on that tree and on
  this patch, so E-044 holds for it.
- Unit tests on 4 GH200 GPUs under torchrun (EP=4): the tests this patch
  adds or changes pass, as do the PR's other overlap and hybrid tests,
  except parametrizations that need 8 GPUs, which stop in
  initialize_model_parallel. The CPU-only tests pass in the container.
- Enabling it requires:
  - comm_overlap.overlap_moe_expert_parallel_comm=true;
  - model.mtp_num_layers=null (MCore and Megatron-Bridge accept only None or
    1 with the overlap, and the Nano recipe sets 0);
  - CUDA_DEVICE_MAX_CONNECTIONS > 1 (32 was used; with a single hardware
    queue the compute and communication streams serialise and the overlap
    gains nothing);
  - none of the refused settings above, and no packed sequences
    (Megatron-Bridge builds the plan without packed_seq_params and refuses
    them).

